WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.330
Shake an alkene with orange-brown
bromine, in the dark, at room temperature.

2
00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:08.050
The colour vanishes almost at once.

3
00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:12.950
An alkane, as you've seen, needs light
before bromine will react with it.

4
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:16.510
So why does an alkene take
bromine's colour away in the dark,

5
00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:18.630
when an alkane needs light?

6
00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:23.710
In this mission, you'll meet electrophiles,
and the addition reactions of alkenes,

7
00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:26.820
including the test for a
carbon–carbon double bond.

8
00:00:26.870 --> 00:00:32.170
You'll add hydrogen halides and water across
the double bond, and name the products.

9
00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:37.410
Your mission: explain why alkenes
decolourize bromine without needing light.
